# The Supabase project that keeps the library.
#
# With these unset the Atlas runs exactly as it always has, on the SQLite file
# in data/ — everything below is opt-in. With them set, the server pulls the
# library down on boot and writes every new source up as it arrives.
#
# The service role key writes. It must never reach a browser: set it on the
# machine that runs the server and nowhere else. The anon key can only read,
# and is the one to use anywhere public.

SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Telling the curator an entry has arrived --------------------------------
#
# A submission from the website is queued, not published, and this is how the
# curator hears about it. Both of the first two have to be set before any mail
# is sent; with either missing the queue still fills and nothing is sent, which
# is a quiet failure rather than a lost entry — the entries are all still there.
#
# ATLAS_MAIL_KEY is an API key from a transactional mail provider (Resend by
# default; anything with the same JSON shape works via ATLAS_MAIL_API). It is a
# secret: the machine that runs the Atlas, and nowhere else.
#
# ATLAS_MAIL_FROM has to be an address the provider has verified. Resend lends
# onboarding@resend.dev to a project with no domain of its own yet, which is the
# default here and is fine to start with.
#
# ATLAS_SITE_URL pins the address the review link points at. Without it the link
# points at whichever deployment answered the request, which on a host that
# builds every push means a preview URL rather than the real one.

ATLAS_MAIL_KEY=
ATLAS_NOTIFY_TO=
ATLAS_MAIL_FROM=Regenerative Atlas <onboarding@resend.dev>
ATLAS_SITE_URL=
